# XCU colon
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/colon.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.colon.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/do nothing except return
class      required
says       The null utility exits with status zero, with or without operands
           and whatever the status before it was.
test       t/001-status.sh

assertion  XCU.colon.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#OPTIONS/Implementations shall not support any options
class      required
since      2024
says       The null utility supports no options and does not treat "--"
           specially: option-like operands and "--" are accepted without a
           diagnostic and with status zero.
test       t/002-no-options.sh

assertion  XCU.colon.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.1
class      required
says       The operands of the null utility are still expanded: an
           assignment made by an expansion in an operand and a command
           substitution in an operand both take effect.
test       t/003-expansions.sh

assertion  XCU.colon.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#STDOUT/Not used
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#STDERR/Not used
class      required
says       The null utility writes nothing to standard output and nothing to
           standard error.
test       t/004-no-output.sh

assertion  XCU.colon.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.2
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXAMPLES/x=y
class      required
says       Being a special built-in, a variable assignment before the null
           utility stays in effect after it, and its redirections are
           performed (a file named in an output redirection is created or
           truncated).
test       t/005-special-builtin.sh

assertion  XCU.colon.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       When the redirection of the null utility fails, a non-interactive
           shell exits with a non-zero status and runs no further command.
test       t/006-redir-error.sh
